# Cashfree credentials — A TEMPLATE. DO NOT PUT REAL KEYS IN THIS FILE.
# ==============================================================================
#
#   ⚠  THIS FILE IS TRACKED BY GIT. Anything typed here is committed, pushed and
#      public. On 28 Sep 2026 live production keys were pasted in here through
#      the GitHub web editor and had to be revoked. Every line below is
#      commented out so that cannot quietly happen again.
#
#   Real keys go in apps/web/.env.local, which is gitignored and exists only on
#   your own machine. Never in here, and never in a chat message.
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#
#   cd <repo>
#   cat .env.cashfree.example >> apps/web/.env.local
#   # now open apps/web/.env.local, UNCOMMENT the lines, and fill them in there
#
#   Then check them:   npm run check:cashfree
#   That reports which of the three products Cashfree accepts, and never prints
#   a secret.
#
# APPEND (>>), NOT COPY (>). apps/web/.env.local already holds your Supabase
# keys, WhatsApp token and everything else; copying over it would wipe them.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THESE ARE THREE DIFFERENT CASHFREE PRODUCTS.
#
# Each has its own dashboard, its own host, and its own key pair. Using the
# payment-gateway App ID for verification or payouts fails with
# "x-client-secret_value_invalid", which reads like a wrong password and is
# actually the wrong product entirely.
#
# SANDBOX KEYS AND PRODUCTION KEYS ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. A production
# secret sent to a sandbox host is rejected, and the error names the secret
# rather than the mismatch. Keep each _ENV line matched to the keys beside it.
# ==============================================================================
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#
#   cd <repo>
#   cat .env.cashfree.example >> apps/web/.env.local
#   # then edit apps/web/.env.local and fill in the values
#
# APPEND (>>), NOT COPY (>). If apps/web/.env.local already exists it holds your
# Supabase keys, WhatsApp token and everything else; copying over it would wipe
# them and the app would stop starting.
#
# apps/web/.env.local is gitignored and must stay that way. Never commit a
# filled-in copy of this file, and never paste these values into a chat — a key
# that has been pasted anywhere should be revoked and regenerated.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THESE ARE THREE DIFFERENT CASHFREE PRODUCTS.
#
# Each has its own dashboard, its own host, and its own key pair. Using the
# payment-gateway App ID for verification or payouts fails with
# "x-client-secret_value_invalid", which reads like a wrong password and is
# actually the wrong product entirely.
# ==============================================================================


# ── 1. Payment gateway (fees, pay-links, refunds) ─────────────────────────────
# Already working in production. Listed so this file is the whole picture.
# Dashboard: PG → Developers → API Keys
# Host: https://sandbox.cashfree.com/pg | https://api.cashfree.com/pg

# CASHFREE_ENV=
# CASHFREE_APP_ID=
# CASHFREE_SECRET_KEY=


# ── 2. Bank account verification (Secure ID / Verification Suite) ─────────────
# Penny-drops an account before the school pays it, and returns the name the
# bank holds — which catches an account that exists but belongs to someone else.
# Dashboard: Verification Suite → Developers → API Keys
# Host: https://sandbox.cashfree.com/verification | https://api.cashfree.com/verification
#
# Leave CASHFREE_VERIFICATION_APP_ID blank and the feature is simply off.
# EVERY CALL IS BILLED, so results are cached against a hash of account+IFSC.
# No account number is ever stored — only a hash and the last four digits.

# CASHFREE_VERIFICATION_ENV=
# CASHFREE_VERIFICATION_APP_ID=
# CASHFREE_VERIFICATION_SECRET_KEY=


# ── 3. Payouts (pay staff and vendors, instead of a NEFT bank file) ───────────
# Dashboard: Payouts → Developers → API Keys
# Host: https://sandbox.cashfree.com/payout | https://api.cashfree.com/payout
#
# CLIENT ID: use the OLDEST client id on the account. A newer one produces
# "Signature Mismatched", which looks like a broken signature and is not.
#
# PUBLIC KEY: Payouts → Developers → Two-Factor Authentication → select
# "Public Key" → Generate Public Key. Paste the WHOLE .pem including the
# -----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY----- and -----END PUBLIC KEY----- lines. Either real
# newlines or \n escapes work. This is required rather than optional: Cloud Run
# has no static IP to allowlist, so public-key 2FA is the only 2FA available.
#
# PREFUNDED WALLET: transfers draw down a balance you top up by NEFT from a
# whitelisted school account (Payouts → Fund Sources). It is not a direct debit
# of the school's bank, so money sits with Cashfree between top-up and payout.

# CASHFREE_PAYOUT_ENV=
# CASHFREE_PAYOUT_CLIENT_ID=
# CASHFREE_PAYOUT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# CASHFREE_PAYOUT_PUBLIC_KEY=

# LEAVE THIS false.
#
# Having the keys is deliberately not enough to move money. The Payouts V2
# request field names could not be confirmed against a live call from the build
# container, so every transfer is refused until this is set by hand.
#
# Before setting it to true:
#   1. fill in the sandbox keys above
#   2. GET /api/payouts?probe=1   (staff session, payroll: view)
#   3. confirm the probe creates a beneficiary and reads a balance
#
# Salary still goes out through the existing NEFT bank file either way — nothing
# in payroll calls payouts yet, and a selftest asserts it stays that way.
# CASHFREE_PAYOUTS_ARMED=


# ==============================================================================
# PRODUCTION IS DIFFERENT — DO NOT PUT SECRETS IN A FILE ON THE SERVER
#
# On Cloud Run the three secrets live in Secret Manager. The non-secret halves
# (APP_ID, CLIENT_ID, the ENV flags, ARMED) are passed by scripts/deploy-online.sh
# from your local .env.local and need nothing further.
#
# Create the secrets:
#
#   printf %s "<verification secret>" | gcloud secrets create \
#     school-erp-cashfree-verification-secret-key --data-file=- \
#     --project=school-erp-prod-493619
#
#   printf %s "<payout client secret>" | gcloud secrets create \
#     school-erp-cashfree-payout-client-secret --data-file=- \
#     --project=school-erp-prod-493619
#
#   gcloud secrets create school-erp-cashfree-payout-public-key \
#     --data-file=/path/to/public_key.pem --project=school-erp-prod-493619
#
# Then add them to the --set-secrets line in cloudbuild.yaml:
#
#   CASHFREE_VERIFICATION_SECRET_KEY=school-erp-cashfree-verification-secret-key:latest
#   CASHFREE_PAYOUT_CLIENT_SECRET=school-erp-cashfree-payout-client-secret:latest
#   CASHFREE_PAYOUT_PUBLIC_KEY=school-erp-cashfree-payout-public-key:latest
#
# THAT LAST STEP IS DELIBERATELY NOT DONE FOR YOU. A secret named in
# --set-secrets that does not exist in Secret Manager fails the WHOLE deploy,
# and these features are off by default — so wiring them in ahead of time would
# break every deploy for a feature nobody had enabled yet. Add each line only
# after its secret exists.
# ==============================================================================
